//! The `field-sizing` [CSS](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/CSS) property enables you
//! to control the sizing behavior of elements that are given a default preferred size, such as form
//! control elements. This property enables you to override the default sizing behavior, allowing
//! form controls to adjust in size to fit their contents.
//!
//! Initial: fixed. Inherited: no.
//! Percentages: not accepted.
//!
//! Grammar: fixed | content
//!
//! Specification: https://drafts.csswg.org/css-forms-1/#propdef-field-sizing
//!
//! Author guide: https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/CSS/Reference/Properties/field-sizing
//!
//! Purpose and value descriptions adapted from MDN contributors (CC-BY-SA-2.5).
//!
//! Generated from @webref/css 8.7.8. Do not edit.

